e denominator of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{w}+1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569969 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "25064e53-93b3-52b6-af27-2a0003a93f3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569969 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{w}-1.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{w}-1,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{w}+1} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{w}+1}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{w}-1}{\\sqrt{w}-1} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{w}-1}{(\\sqrt{w}+1)(\\sqrt{w}-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{w}-1}{(\\sqrt{w})^{2}-{1}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{w}-1}{w-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569985 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186569918 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569985 #edb/ref 1069 "q-34859" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569985 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569985 #edb/ref 1071 "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{x}{7+\\sqrt{x-5}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569985 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4de4e407-29f5-567d-8ce6-c2253af336bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569985 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $7-\\sqrt{x-5}.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $7-\\sqrt{x-5},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{7+\\sqrt{x-5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x}{7+\\sqrt{x-5}}\\cdot \\frac{7-\\sqrt{x-5}}{7-\\sqrt{x-5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x(7-\\sqrt{x-5})}{(7+\\sqrt{x-5})(7-\\sqrt{x-5})} & = \\\\ \\frac{7x-x\\sqrt{x-5}}{{7}^{2}-(\\sqrt{x-5})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{7x-x\\sqrt{x-5}}{49-(x-5)} & = \\\\ \\frac{7x-x\\sqrt{x-5}}{54-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569992 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186569886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569992 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111087" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569992 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186569992 #edb/ref 10