\\sqrt{x-3}+\\sqrt{x-2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{x-3}+\\sqrt{x-2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{x-3}-\\sqrt{x-2}}{\\sqrt{x-3}-\\sqrt{x-2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(\\sqrt{x-3}-\\sqrt{x-2})}{(\\sqrt{x-3}+\\sqrt{x-2})(\\sqrt{x-3}-\\sqrt{x-2})} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(\\sqrt{x-3}-\\sqrt{x-2})}{(\\sqrt{x-3})^{2}-(\\sqrt{x-2})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(\\sqrt{x-3}-\\sqrt{x-2})}{x-3-(x-2)} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(\\sqrt{x-3}-\\sqrt{x-2})}{-1} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{x-2}-3\\sqrt{x-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570031 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186569880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570031 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111070" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570031 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570031 #edb/ref 1071 "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t}+2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570031 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dad03d87-b391-52d0-a812-6cdef4bf6aad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570031 #edb/ref 1074 "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{t}-2.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{t}-2,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t}+2} & = \\\\ \\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t}+2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{t}-2}{\\sqrt{t}-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{t(\\sqrt{t}-2)}{(\\sqrt{t}+2)(\\sqrt{t}-2)} & = \\\\ \\frac{t(\\sqrt{t}-2)}{(\\sqrt{t})^{2}-{2}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{t(\\sqrt{t}-2)}{t-4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
